.TH PSSaveDataToFile 3 2023-12-03 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSSaveDataToFile

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/dataset.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSSaveDataToFile\fR(\fIconst char *path\fR, \fIPSFloat *data\fR, \fIuint64_t len\fR, \fIint opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Save dataset \fIdata\fR to the file located at \fIpath\fR. The dataset must be an array of PSFloat elements whose length (number of elements) defined by argument \fIlen\fR.
.br
By default, the dataset is saved as a comma-separated list of its values written as string representations of floating point numbers.
.br
The datasets itself is prefixed with its length written as a string representation of a decimal number followed by a colon separator caharcter (':').
.br
Example: 3:1.25,2,-0.15 (dataset of three elements 1.25, 2.0 and -0.15) If flag \fIPS_IO_BINARY_MODE\fR is set into \fIopts\fR, the dataset will be saved in binary format.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
1 if datasets is successfully saved, 0 in case of failure.
Possible failure reasons:
.br

.RS 4
\[bu] Mandatory arguments \fIpath\fR or \fIdata\fR are \fINULL\fR.
.br

\[bu] File at \fIpath\fR cannot be opened for writing.
.br

\[bu] Some error occurs while writing to the file.
.br
.RE
